From 8fcd5c1a1bde8adc846710b57b3583ac27c5a76a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Philip Mueller <claude@philipmueller.ch>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 09:17:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/31] feat(harbor_agent): OpenCode agent on the Gym model
 server; capture-aware masking

custom_agents/opencode_nemo_gym.py: OpenCodeNemoGym subclasses Harbor's
installed OpenCode agent (Harbor 9dddd797 knows only hosted providers) and
declares one @ai-sdk/openai-compatible provider whose baseURL is harbor_agent's
api_base, passed via OPENCODE_CONFIG_CONTENT; small_model uses the same
endpoint. OpenCode runs in the sandbox, so api_base must be reachable from
there (harbor_model_base_url).

app.py: with training-token capture enabled, an empty output list no longer
masks the rollout (OpenCode writes no ATIF; the model server holds the tokens
and masks on its own when no call chain was captured). Failed trials and trials
without a verifier result stay masked.

Harbor 0.25: installed agents no longer return `ExecInput` lists from
`create_run_agent_commands` for the base class to run; they implement
`install()`/`run()` themselves, and `exec_as_agent` raises on a non-zero exit
(harbor agents/installed/base.py:999-1083). New `installed_compat.py` keeps
the old contract for our adapters: `ExecInput`, `run_commands` (one recorded
command under command-<i>/, exit status recorded, not raised) and
`install_from_template`. Harbor 0.25 also rejects agent kwargs its
options_model lacks (agents/base.py:283-305), so the kwargs harbor_agent gives
every agent (`responses_create_params`, `temperature`) and the Terminus-2
options of the shared harbor_agent_kwargs (`interleaved_thinking`,
`max_turns`, `model_info`) are dropped before Harbor sees them. Harbor 0.25's
OpenCode would write an ATIF trajectory from opencode.txt; this agent keeps
writing none. The npm install is Harbor 0.25's, so the run command sources nvm
first as Harbor's own OpenCode run does.

Signed-off-by: Philip Mueller <claude@philipmueller.ch>
